  "behavior_shift": "v2 floored arm folds MORE facing action at EVERY depth (e.g. 0-4bb 0.571 vs 0.388; 15-25bb 0.683 vs 0.603) and carries LESS allin mass at 10-25bb (0.095-0.115 vs 0.143-0.144) than deployed \u2014 broad-spectrum tightening, not depth-localized (unpaired, self-play envs differ)",
  "g3_by_level": "deficit sits at L3-L7 (mid depths, -0.03..-0.16), positive at L8 (+0.36) \u2014 same shape as the paired decomposition"
 },
 "answers": {
  "q1_does_deficit_concentrate_at_shallow": "NO \u2014 inverted. v2 GAINS at the shallow terminal depths where the champion's depth confusion lives (<=6bb: +0.130/game, z=+11.8, broad across 15/19 profiles) and LOSES at mid depths 6-25bb (z=-6.4 and -4.4). The killphilmtt deficit specifically is depth-FLAT (no bucket beyond |z|=0.61).",
  "q2_fork_verdict": "BOTH branches are true, for different parts of the failure: (i) for the killphilmtt gate criterion, depth confusion was NOT the EV-binding defect \u2014 a provably depth-cured encoder left the hole exactly unchanged at every depth (paired z=-0.86; G1b floor value did not collapse, +0.320 diverged-only, run-best); the hole is a policy defect. (ii) the gate failures that ARE movement (panel profile structure, G3 2.55sigma) trace to an INDEPENDENT broad-spectrum regression: uniform tightening/passivity producing significant mid-depth (6-25bb) losses vs pressure profiles, offset by genuine shallow gains. Net z=-0.54 hides two opposite-signed depth-localized effects.",
  "q3_f_pillar_implication": "KEEP the bbnorm encoder in the organ bank, upgraded from 'representationally clean' to 'economically signed at shallow': the +0.130/game <=6bb paired gain is exactly where the depth cure should bite, and is broad across profiles. The mid-depth tightening and killphil hole are policy/run-level, not encoder-level (G4 confirms live-servability). Caveat: encoder and run are confounded (single seed, G=12); the shallow gain could in principle be run-specific. Cheapest disambiguation: per-hand logging fix above + one champion-recipe/original-encoder rerun under the same seeds."
 }
